# No AI agent attribution

Never put AI tool or model names in git history, PRs, docs, comments, or metadata.

## Forbidden

- `Co-authored-by:` trailers for Cursor, Claude, Copilot, ChatGPT, Composer, or any AI agent/model
- Footers like `Generated by …`, `Written with …`, `Via Cursor/Claude`
- Listing AI tools as authors, contributors, or co-authors in `gemspec`, README, CHANGELOG, LICENSE, or GitHub release notes

## Required

- Commits use only the human author's name/email from `git config`
- Commit messages are Conventional Commits with no AI marketing or tool branding
- If a skill or default suggests adding AI `Co-authored-by`, **ignore it** for this repo

## Examples

```text
# ❌ BAD
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

# ✅ GOOD
(no co-author trailer; commit as the human maintainer only)
```
